<title>BRAZIL: FORECAST- Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</title>
<headline>FORECAST- Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are consensus forecasts from a survey of economic indicators taken from eight Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro brokerages and research firms. Also included are current market rates for dollar and interest rate futures over the next three months.</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>*****Brazil Indicators - April Consensus Forecast*****</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>INDICATOR	  PERIOD     AVG FORCST    MEDIAN     PRVS MO</p>
<p>CPI (Fipe)	  April	0.54 pct     0.55 pct   0.21 pct</p>
<p>PPI (IPA-M/FGV)   April	0.30 pct     0.35 pct   1.62 pct</p>
<p>Inflation (IGP-M) April	0.37 pct     0.35 pct   1.15 pct</p>
<p>Ind Act (IBGE)    March	  N.A.	 N.A.	 2.90 pct</p>
<p>Trade Balance     April     -$660 million    -$675 million  -$1.02 bln</p>
<p>Exports	     April	$4.20 bln    $4.22 bln  $3.83 bln</p>
<p>Imports	     April	$4.86 bln    $4.88 bln  $4.85 bln</p>
<p>				   ******</p>
<p>		Brazilian Financial Indicators</p>
<p>	  Futures market rates at April 15 close</p>
<p>			 April	    May	    June</p>
<p>Real/Dollar	   1.0659	   1.0739	 1.0820</p>
<p>Monthly Int Rates   1.667 pct	1.594 pct    1.582 pct</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTES: Price indicators reflect monthly variation.</p>
<p>Industrial activity reflects annual variation.</p>
<p>((-- John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414))</p>
